
post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'

Magnetar repository configuration installed.

  Drop-ins:      /etc/pacman.d/magnetar-repos.d/
  Canonical:     /usr/share/magnetar/pacman.conf
                 (magnetar-pacman-conf renders it for this CPU)
  Policy:        https://github.com/Magnetar-OS/magnetar/blob/main/docs/REPOS.md

/etc/pacman.conf was NOT modified. On an existing system, review the canonical
file, rendered with the optimised repositories this CPU can run, against yours
and adopt it deliberately:

  diff -u /etc/pacman.conf <(magnetar-pacman-conf)

Repository ORDER in that file is a hard priority — pacman takes each package
from the first repo that carries it and ignores newer builds below. Reordering
the sections is how a system silently gets re-sourced from someone else's
build farm. Read the policy before you do.

Verify the result at any time with:

  magnetar-repo-audit

Third-party repositories ship DISABLED. A repository's keyring lives inside
the repository it verifies, so it cannot be a dependency of this package —
enabling has to import a key first, and that should be deliberate:

  magnetar-repo status
  magnetar-repo enable chaotic-aur
  magnetar-repo enable endeavouros
  magnetar-repo enable valve        (stays locked: Usage = Sync Search)

Enabling one late cannot change its priority: order is fixed by the number in
its filename, and every file there sorts below the Arch repositories.

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  # The drop-ins are backup= files, so pacman handles them. The canonical
  # pacman.conf is the one that can drift, and only the machine's owner can
  # decide how to merge it. Compared as rendered for this CPU, so a machine
  # the installer set up stays quiet until the canonical file really changes.
  if ! magnetar-pacman-conf 2>/dev/null | diff -q /etc/pacman.conf - >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    cat <<'MSG'

magnetar-repos: /etc/pacman.conf differs from the canonical file shipped in this
version. That may be entirely intentional — your locks live there too. Review
when convenient:

  diff -u /etc/pacman.conf <(magnetar-pacman-conf)

MSG
  fi
}
